    "id": "rate_half_list_budget_three_antipodal_generic_deleted_pair_torsion_cyclotomic_norm_decomposition",
    "title": "Budget-three deleted-pair torsion cyclotomic-norm decomposition",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "For every dyadic M, the squared Jacobi/Chebyshev torsion resultants are exact cyclotomic norms: the T_(2M) branch is one Phi_(8M) norm and the U_(2M-1) branch is the product of the dyadic norm tower Phi_4 through Phi_(4M). The plus branch is equivalently (2M)^M times the product of resultants against T_1,T_2,...,T_M; over Q(sqrt(2)) the minus branch is the product of two conjugate resultants against sqrt(2)T_M+/-1. Odd-prime norm valuations are twice the resultant valuations. At official M=2^35 neither modular torsion factor need exceed degree M, without asserting modular nonvanishing.",
